  85:app/prog/dbus/dbusdllXs.c **** /**
  86:app/prog/dbus/dbusdllXs.c **** By default a physical node (communication partner) reacts only to one node address. It is, however,
  87:app/prog/dbus/dbusdllXs.c **** The default implementation (containing only one node address) can be replaced by a function, which 
  88:app/prog/dbus/dbusdllXs.c **** 
  89:app/prog/dbus/dbusdllXs.c **** \note Scenario: Electronic node answers to node address: 1 and Ah (decimal: 10).
  90:app/prog/dbus/dbusdllXs.c **** When addressing node 1 an acknowledgment from node 1 is sent
  91:app/prog/dbus/dbusdllXs.c **** When addressing node Ah an acknowledgment from node Ah is sent.
  92:app/prog/dbus/dbusdllXs.c **** 
  93:app/prog/dbus/dbusdllXs.c **** Furthermore, it is possible to implement a subsystem differentiation by adapting this function here
  94:app/prog/dbus/dbusdllXs.c **** if ((ucAddress & 0xF6)== 0xA0).
  95:app/prog/dbus/dbusdllXs.c **** 
  96:app/prog/dbus/dbusdllXs.c **** \return
  97:app/prog/dbus/dbusdllXs.c ****  \b type: bool\n
  98:app/prog/dbus/dbusdllXs.c ****  \b range \li 0 = false
  99:app/prog/dbus/dbusdllXs.c ****           \li all other values = true
 100:app/prog/dbus/dbusdllXs.c **** */
